    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **56 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field, derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane), as an IANA name.\n\nThe `OwnerDto` is generated at build time from the OpenAPI spec, and derived fields are computed in the MapStruct mapper \u2014 so the change spans three files:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `timezone` string property to the `Owner` schema, next to the existing `locality`, so the generated DTO exposes it.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/OwnerTimezone.java`** (new) \u2014 a small helper mirroring the existing `OwnerRegion` pattern, mapping a region code to its IANA timezone (returning `null` for `UNKNOWN`/unmapped regions, so the field is simply absent for those owners).\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `timezone` mapping that reuses the existing `deriveLocality(owner)` (which already resolves the region from the customerCode prefix, falling back to postcode/city), so `timezone` stays consistent with `locality`.\n\nThe driving spec test `Cp42Tests` (Sydney \u2192 locality `NSW`, timezone `Australia/Sydney`) passes, along with the existing locality tests and the entire suite.",
